190: \item \textbf{Constant Sweep Rate FORC (V71)}: introduced the \code{--forc\_rate} parameter to dynamically scale cycle durations (ramp-up and ramp-down times) proportionally to curve depth (Method B from \code{FORC.md}), keeping the sweep rate $dB/dt \equiv R$ constant across curves and avoiding the variable sweep rate trap;
191: \item \textbf{Biaxial Rotational Demagnetization (V72)}: replaced the uniaxial sinusoidal decaying field (AFD) with a biaxial rotational demagnetization protocol (Method A from \code{compass\_sim\_protocol\_notes.md}), where the field rotates in the $xy$-plane while decaying linearly to zero, providing an isotropic randomized demagnetized state ($S \to 0$);
192: \item \textbf{Hysteresis Autoscale Default (V73)}: changed the default value of the \code{--hyst\_autoscale} parameter from 0 to 1 (True) to enable automatic scaling of the MxH axes by default;
193: \item \textbf{Simulated Thermal Annealing Demagnetization (V74)}: implemented Method B (linear sweep with decaying simulated thermal annealing white noise torque) as an alternative pre-treatment demagnetization protocol, and introduced the temperature scaling parameter \code{--demag\_temp};
